---
description: Test conventions — levels, markers, fixtures, invariants
globs: tests/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Where tests go
- `tests/` (existing 1.x suite): keep green. Do not restructure.
- `tests/v2/` for all 2.0 work, mirroring the package:
  `tests/v2/services/test_event_log.py` tests `iterthink/services/event_log.py`.
- `tests/v2/architecture/`: static checks on the codebase. Allowlists only shrink.
- `tests/v2/contract/`: human-owned behaviour of the bridge, run against the
  fake and the real implementation. Never edit; make implementations pass.
- `tests/v2/invariants/`: property-based tests (Hypothesis) for the rules
  below. Every invariant gets at least one.

# Levels and markers (registered in `tests/v2/conftest.py`)
- no marker = unit: pure, in-memory or `tmp_path`, < 100 ms each.
- `@pytest.mark.integration`: real files, real SQLite, several modules.
- `@pytest.mark.jj`: needs the `jj` binary; use the `jj_bin` fixture.
- `@pytest.mark.slow`: > 1 s. Only `--full` runs them.
- `@pytest.mark.e2e`: FastAPI TestClient through a full user flow.
- `@pytest.mark.network`: allowed to open non-loopback sockets. Avoid; the
  default blocks them and the test fails loudly.

# Fixtures to use, not reinvent
- `project_dir`: a fresh project folder with a `.md`, a `.csv` and a
  subfolder. Treat its source files as user data: tests assert they are
  unchanged unless a proposal was accepted.
- `source_snapshot(project_dir)`: hashes of all source files; compare before
  and after.
- `jj_bin`: path to jj, or skip (local) / fail (CI, `ITERTHINK_REQUIRE_JJ=1`).
- `fixed_clock`: deterministic timestamps for event tests.
- LLM calls: use a fake router returning canned text. Never call Ollama or a
  cloud model in tests.

# Invariants that must always have tests
1. Rebuild equals incremental: feeding the same logs in shuffled arrival order
   gives the same index as a full rebuild.
2. Hash chain: altering, removing or reordering any line makes verification
   fail at that line; an untouched log verifies.
3. Source files are untouched unless a proposal was accepted.
4. Nothing is applied without a verdict event.
5. Events are idempotent: replaying a log twice changes nothing.
6. Egress `none`: no remote call is attempted (assert on the fake router).
7. Projects never mix: queries for project A return nothing from project B.
8. Conflicts are surfaced, never resolved silently.

# Style
- Arrange / act / assert, one behaviour per test, name says the behaviour:
  `test_reject_keeps_candidate_commit`.
- Golden files under `tests/v2/golden/` for HTML fragments and diffs; update
  only with `--update-golden` and mention it in the slice.
- No sleeps. Use events, fakes or `fixed_clock`.
- A bug fix starts with a failing test that reproduces it.
